# .agent-work/ is TRACKED: run artifacts, verdicts, lessons and archives are
# durable project history, not scratch. Transient bits stay excluded below.
.agent-work/**/__pycache__/
.agent-work/**/*.pyc
.agent-work/**/.pytest_cache/
# Live runtime state, not run history: per-session governor readings and the
# active-session registry are rewritten constantly and are machine-specific.
# Engine journals are NOT excluded - they are the tamper-evident audit trail.
.agent-work/**/gauge.json
.agent-work/**/gauge-skip.json
.agent-work/.spine-rail-binding.json
.agent-work/.spine-rail-nudges.json
# Captured eval workspaces embed a full copy of another checkout's skills tree.
# They are a copied checkout, not run history, and their nesting exceeds the
# Windows path limit -- `git worktree add` fails with 'Filename too long'.
.agent-work/**/constellation-eval-*/
# Same defect, general shape: a captured checkout nests a SECOND .agent-work/
# inside this one. The `constellation-eval-*` rule above only matched captures
# named that way; a RED-reproduction capture under a work area slipped past it
# and landed at 216 characters -- past the Windows limit, so every test running
# `git worktree add` died with exit 128 ('Filename too long').
# This rule is prevention only: it does not untrack the pre-existing captures
# under .agent-work/dispatch-126-127/, which are already tracked history and sit
# under the limit. Exclude the copied checkout, never the run that captured it.
.agent-work/**/.agent-work/
# Per-machine hook wiring (#539). `install_constellation.py --wire-hooks
# --hooks-from source` writes this file: it carries THIS checkout's absolute
# paths and the interpreter name probed on THIS host, so it is wrong for every
# other machine by construction. .claude/settings.json stays tracked and shared;
# Claude Code merges the hooks from both rather than letting one replace the
# other. The installer refuses outright to write this file if it is git-tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.coverage
junit*.xml
# Defensive: eval run-dirs are fabricated under the system temp dir (never the
# repo tree); this only fires if a run is ever redirected into evals/ (#106).
evals/**/_runs/
# Rebuilt intermediates of the derived code map (issue #456). Both are
# regenerated from source by `python -m scripts.code_map build`, so committing
# them would commit a second copy of the repo that goes stale on the next edit.
# Narrow by file, not a blanket .code-map/ rule: a later gate may add a store
# that has to be reviewed.
.code-map/statements.jsonl
# The run reports are rebuilt beside the store on every run. Listed one per
# line for the same reason: a blanket rule would also swallow a store a later
# gate wants reviewed.
.code-map/extract_report.json
.code-map/render_report.json
# The page tree under map/ is regenerated the same way and mostly stays
# untracked for the same reason -- committing 4,000+ generated pages doubles
# the repo and goes stale on every edit. Only the 2-file entry point ships:
# map/INDEX.md + map/ids.jsonl, measured stable under a body-edit/shape-edit
# arm pair (.agent-work/issue-456/landing-zone-measurement.md). The
# `map_tree_freshness` test in tests/test_code_map.py is what keeps those two
# tracked files honest against the untracked rest.
map/*
!map/INDEX.md
!map/ids.jsonl
.claude/skills/
.claude/settings.local.json
